From 5b5e33bdacb59b9cf534729c74126c94e2e8b595 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gabriel Fernandez <gabriel.fernandez@foss.st.com>
Date: Thu, 18 Apr 2024 09:54:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 197/913] clk: stm32mp21: add clock dependency from BSEC DENR

The CoreSight devices can be accesses only when BSEC_DENR:DBGSWEN
is set, otherwise a bus-error occurs.
To prevent Linux from accessing unavailable CoreSight devices,
make the exported SCMI clock of the CoreSight bus clock depending
from BSEC_DENR:DBGSWEN.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git 4cf8dc9688c0a71af82f11d20660a905f80ad9eb clk: stm32mp21: add clock dependency from BSEC DENR]
Signed-off-by: Antonio Borneo <antonio.borneo@foss.st.com>
Signed-off-by: Gabriel Fernandez <gabriel.fernandez@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: I5992c4f12c0654fb0eefb27ec14b1b2ab2653706
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/optee_os/+/374581
---
 core/drivers/clk/clk-stm32mp21.c | 237 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 188 insertions(+), 49 deletions(-)

